{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-1","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-1","text":"AGENTS.md — orientation for agents working in this repository"}]},{"id":"blk-2","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2","marks":["bold"],"text":"Audited against the tree 2026-08-15; re-audited 2026-09-19."},{"id":"spn-3","text":" Everything below was checked by running the command or opening the file, not carried forward from the previous version of this document. What the previous version got wrong is retracted by name at the bottom — that section is the useful part of this file for anyone who read it before today."}]},{"id":"blk-3","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-4","marks":["code"],"text":"CLAUDE.md"},{"id":"spn-5","text":" is the longer, authoritative brief and is injected into every session automatically. This file is the short orientation for agents that read "},{"id":"spn-6","marks":["code"],"text":"AGENTS.md"},{"id":"spn-7","text":" by convention. "},{"id":"spn-8","marks":["bold"],"text":"Where the two disagree, `CLAUDE.md` wins"},{"id":"spn-9","text":" — and tell someone, because they should not disagree."}]},{"id":"blk-4","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-10","text":"What this repository is"}]},{"id":"blk-5","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-11","text":"A multi-project portfolio for the [&] Protocol ecosystem: a protocol spec, reference implementations, an operating system, a governance kernel, "},{"id":"spn-12","marks":["bold"],"text":"~46 sub-repositories"},{"id":"spn-13","text":" and **18 "},{"id":"spn-14","marks":["code"],"text":"*.com"},{"id":"spn-15","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-16","marks":["code"],"text":"*.org"},{"id":"spn-17","text":" directories"},{"id":"spn-18","marks":["bold"],"text":" (counted 2026-09-19; this said ~27 and ~15, which was the April tree). "},{"id":"spn-19","text":"The parent repo tracks almost none of the sub-repos** — commit and push "},{"id":"spn-20","marks":["italic"],"text":"inside"},{"id":"spn-21","text":" the sub-repo, never by bumping a gitlink in the parent."}]},{"id":"blk-6","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22","marks":["bold"],"text":"Before non-trivial work, read `STACK_COMPLETION.md`"},{"id":"spn-23","text":" — it is the canonical answer to \"where are we?\" — and then "},{"id":"spn-24","marks":["code"],"text":"REVISION_REGISTER.md"},{"id":"spn-25","text":", which lists what in the tree still contradicts a decision already made. Do not trust an undated planning document in here."}]},{"id":"blk-7","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-26","text":"Where the real code is"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-9","spans":[{"id":"spn-27","text":"Path"}]},{"id":"blk-10","spans":[{"id":"spn-28","text":"What it is"}]}],"id":"blk-8","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-11","spans":[{"id":"spn-29","marks":["code"],"text":"super/"}]},{"id":"blk-12","spans":[{"id":"spn-30","marks":["bold"],"text":"Super (CD)"},{"id":"spn-31","text":" — desktop cockpit + "},{"id":"spn-32","marks":["code"],"text":"ampd"},{"id":"spn-33","text":" authority runtime, the app this stack is built "},{"id":"spn-34","marks":["italic"],"text":"with"},{"id":"spn-35","text":". The most active repo in the tree. The working lane lives in two clones outside this tree; see "},{"id":"spn-36","marks":["code"],"text":"CLAUDE.md"},{"id":"spn-37","text":"."}]}],[{"id":"blk-13","spans":[{"id":"spn-38","marks":["code"],"text":"wek/"}]},{"id":"blk-14","spans":[{"id":"spn-39","text":"World Enforcement Kernel — authority, write boundary, verifier, fault harness."}]}],[{"id":"blk-15","spans":[{"id":"spn-40","marks":["code"],"text":"computedriven/"}]},{"id":"blk-16","spans":[{"id":"spn-41","marks":["bold"],"text":"ComputeDriven Edge"},{"id":"spn-42","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-43","marks":["code"],"text":"cd-kernellet"},{"id":"spn-44","text":" floor + FCB competitive benchmark (Rust). Busiest repo by commit count."}]}],[{"id":"blk-17","spans":[{"id":"spn-45","marks":["code"],"text":"RRABBIT/"}]},{"id":"blk-18","spa